From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:08:28 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] atari-carts

Atari 2600 and 7800 carts are drawn in the retro bitmap renderer (ADR
0054) as two shells of the same size, 82 by 98 mm (seated 240x287):
Atari Corp. made its 7800 carts in the same shell size as the 2600 ones
(Video Game Critic, 7800 page; AtariAge forum "will 7800 cartridge
shells work for 2600 games"). The 2600 cart is the Atari Inc. shell, a
ribbed grip across the top above the label well, in black 0x22 0x21
0x22. The 7800 cart is the Atari Corp. shell, a raised top cap and grip
ridges down both sides, the label well higher, in a lighter black 0x2c
0x2c 0x2e. A shell colour chosen in Config/cart_shell.txt still wins.

The outlines and relief are ours (a2600_cart.svg, a7800_cart.svg and
their detail SVGs), lit into a2600_neutral.png and a7800_neutral.png by
examples/retro_neutrals.rs; every other neutral regenerates byte for
byte. The shelf render test lays its sheet out in rows of four.
